{"applies":"svelte 5, sveltekit 2","base":"https://svelte.dev/docs","rows":[
["Runes","Use $state for reactive values","State declared with the rune is a plain value to read and assign.","Declare with $state and assign directly.","Use the old let-with-compiler magic in new code.","let count=$state(0)","let count=0","High","/svelte/$state"],
["Runes","Use $derived for computed values","A derived value updates when its sources change and has no side effects.","Write the expression in $derived.","Recompute in an effect.","let total=$derived(items.reduce((s,i)=>s+i.p,0))","$effect(()=>{total=sum(items)})","High","/svelte/$derived"],
["Runes","Use $derived.by for multi-line logic","A function body avoids awkward ternaries.","Use .by for loops.","Cram a long chain into one line.","let r=$derived.by(()=>{...return x})","$derived(a?b?c:d:e)","Low","/svelte/$derived"],
["Runes","Treat $effect as an escape hatch","Effects run after DOM updates for outside systems.","Use effects for canvas, timers, logging.","Use effects to sync state to state.","$effect(()=>{document.title=title})","$effect(()=>{b=a*2})","High","/svelte/$effect"],
["Runes","Return cleanup from effects","Teardown runs before re-run and on destroy.","Return a function.","Leak timers.","$effect(()=>{const id=setInterval(f,1e3);return()=>clearInterval(id)})","$effect(()=>{setInterval(f,1e3)})","High","/svelte/$effect#Teardown"],
["Runes","Read props through $props","Props arrive as one destructured rune call.","Destructure with defaults.","Use export let in runes mode.","let {title,size='md'}=$props()","export let title","Medium","/svelte/$props"],
["Runes","Bind two-way only with $bindable","A parent can bind only props the child marks bindable.","Mark it and keep the use small.","Mutate props without opting in.","let {value=$bindable()}=$props()","props.value='x'","Medium","/svelte/$bindable"],
["Runes","Avoid mutating props objects","Passing state down to be changed in the child hides data flow.","Use callback props.","Rewrite parent state in the child.","<Child onsave={save}/>","child.items.push(x)","Medium","/svelte/$props"],
["Runes","Use $state.raw for large replace-only data","Deep proxies cost memory on big objects.","Use raw and reassign.","Proxy a huge fetched payload.","let rows=$state.raw([])","let rows=$state(big)","Low","/svelte/$state#$state.raw"],
["Runes","Use $inspect in development only","It logs reactive changes and is stripped from production.","Use it to debug.","Ship console.log in effects.","$inspect(count)","$effect(()=>console.log(count))","Low","/svelte/$inspect"],
